            0.081
          ],
          "content": "Lines and Angles"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.121,
            0.387,
            0.143
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Unlabelled protractor"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.151,
            0.834,
            0.172
          ],
          "content": "Here is a protractor. Do you see the straight angle at the center"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.173,
            0.399,
            0.263
          ],
          "content": "divided into 180 units of 1 degree? Only part of the lines dividing the straight angle are visible, though!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.265,
            0.4,
            0.423
          ],
          "content": "Starting from the marking on the rightmost point of the base, there is a long mark for every $1 0 ^ { \\circ }$ . From every such long mark, there is a medium sized mark after $5 ^ { \\circ }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.407,
            0.181,
            0.857,
            0.358
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_22_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.434,
            0.298,
            0.457
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it out"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.482,
            0.476,
            0.886
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.117,
                0.638,
                0.133,
                0.653
              ],
              "content": "A"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_22_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.487,
            0.469,
            0.833,
            0.513
          ],
          "content": "Write the measures of the following angles:"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.57,
            0.521,
            0.664,
            0.54
          ],
          "content": "a.  \\angle  KAL",
          "image_source": "images/page_22_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.487,
            0.544,
            0.835,
            0.679
          ],
          "content": "Notice that the vertex of this angle coincides with the centre of the protractor. So the number of units of 1 degree angle between KA and AL gives the measure of ∠KAL. By counting, we get —"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.574,
            0.68,
            0.69,
            0.699
          ],
          "content": "\\angle KAL = 30^{\\circ}",
          "image_source": "images/page_22_equation_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.487,
            0.703,
            0.834,
            0.791
          ],
          "content": "Making use of the medium sized and large sized marks, is it possible to count the number of units in 5s or 10s?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.571,
            0.8,
            0.665,
            0.819
          ],
          "content": "b. $\\angle \\mathrm { W A L }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.572,
            0.828,
            0.66,
            0.848
          ],
          "content": "$\\mathtt { C } .$ $\\angle \\mathrm { T A K }$",
          "image_source": "images/page_22_equation_15.jpg"
        },
        {
